content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-108, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23110, on the raw-water transfer line.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal leakage is confirmed by the reported drip of about one drop every two seconds. The troubleshooting table identifies this symptom and requires mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check; it provides no numerical allowable leakage rate, so the drip rate cannot be compared with a documented numerical leak limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable vibration limits are Figure 3's bearing-housing vibration-velocity zones, expressed in mm/s RMS. If the reported 3.2 mm/s is a valid RMS housing measurement, it falls in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C restricted-operation boundary and the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary; it is not in Zone D, where damage is likely and the instruction is to stop the pump. Classification remains provisional because condition monitoring requires readings on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable drive-end bearing-housing surface-temperature limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reported 68 C is within the normal range: 2 C below the normal upper limit, 12 C below alarm and 22 C below trip. It does not meet the troubleshooting symptom of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the supplied and provisionally classified readings, neither the Figure 3 Zone D stop condition nor the 90 C temperature trip is met, so an immediate stop is not supported by those limits. Plan P2 seal repairs for the active leakage rather than treating the Zone B vibration and normal temperature as emergency conditions; the pump must nevertheless never be run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Leading asset-specific suspect, conditional on the original seal still being fitted: early failure of component seal HF3-450. The service bulletin reports such failures on pumps built from serial HF3-22000, caused by a revised sleeve tolerance; P-108's serial HF3-23110 is within that population. Confirm the installed seal type during disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented causes to investigate are worn or cracked seal faces, seal dry-running and shaft misalignment. Inspect the removed seal, establish whether Plan 11 flush was ever lost, and check alignment; the reported vibration and temperature alone do not establish bearing wear as the cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before intervention, verify that the 3.2 mm/s reading is vibration velocity in mm/s RMS on a bearing housing. Measure both bearing housings and classify the highest valid reading with Figure 3; record the housing-surface temperature and confirm the seal-leak location and Plan 11 flush status.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before starting mechanical-seal replacement. Do not run the pump dry while it is isolated, drained or otherwise without seal flush.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment; its documented mass is 68 kg. The back pull-out design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve. Identify whether the removed seal is HF3-450 or HF3-450B, inspect the seal faces, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. Fit one new pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket as required by the seal-replacement procedure. The exemption from seal-setting measurement does not eliminate the preceding sleeve-scoring inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten fasteners using the Table 5 conditions for lightly oiled threads, except where the bulletin supersedes the manual: impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm; bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm where disturbed; and HF3-450B seal gland nuts M10 to 30 Nm, not the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as part of the leakage corrective action. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Apply tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, restore the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run dry. After return to service, check for recurring shaft-seal leakage and housing temperature, and measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings; classify the highest reading using Figure 3 and act on its zone. Continue the documented weekly vibration monitoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one as the one-for-one replacement for the manual's single HF3-450 seal. Mandatory substitute for this in-scope serial; do not fit HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Fit a new gasket during seal replacement; the parts list also requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft-sleeve requirement: make one available or order one only when inspection shows scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth. No scoring depth is available before disassembly.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before seal-replacement work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Plan a lifting-equipment lift for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; lifting equipment is expressly required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain and restore Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge as applicable, and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard labour allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard labour allowance, when performed for the alignment check or required because the motor or bearing housing was moved: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. P-108 is HF3-23110, so the bulletin applies to this asset and supersedes those seal-part and gland-torque entries; the below-serial-HF3-22000 instruction to retain HF3-450 and Table 5 does not apply. The other Table 5 torque values remain applicable.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual procedure 5.2 requires sleeve inspection but gives no numerical scoring limit. For this bulletin-covered serial, use the bulletin's specific rule: replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. The statement that the pre-set HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement removes the seal-setting measurement, not the required inspection for sleeve scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 3.2 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity measurement on a bearing housing, and what is the reading on the other bearing housing? The highest valid housing reading is needed for definitive Figure 3 classification (C06, C07).",
    "Which seal is currently installed, HF3-450 or HF3-450B, and is there any history of Plan 11 flush loss, dry running or misalignment? These facts are needed to test the leading early-failure and troubleshooting hypotheses (C02, C09, C13).",
    "What scoring depth, if any, is found on shaft sleeve HF3-455 during disassembly? This determines whether the conditional sleeve is actually required; the replacement criterion is scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth (C10, C13).",
    "What numerical seal-leakage acceptance criterion, if any, applies after repair? The evidence identifies shaft-seal leakage and its corrective action but supplies neither an allowable drip rate nor a zero-leak acceptance requirement (C09).",
    "The evidence does not provide site-specific lockout/tagging steps, isolation points, permits, PPE or raw-water exposure controls; these must be established separately rather than inferred. Only isolate/drain, lifting and no-dry-run controls are documented here (C02, C10).",
    "No separate HF3-450B cartridge-installation procedure is supplied beyond its pre-set status, prohibition on HF3-450, gland torque and sleeve-scoring rule. Any additional cartridge-specific manufacturer instructions must be obtained if required rather than guessed (C10, C13)."
  ]
}
